 ### GPU Voxel Terrain Generation and Culling Pipeline
-A real-time rendering pipeline that generates voxel terrain on the GPU, culls occluded voxels, and renders them using indirect instanced drawing [S1, unofficial]. It generates terrain as a giant array of voxels every frame, culls voxels by checking if they have all opaque neighbours, and uses `DrawIndirect` to render voxels. The fragment shader computes vertex locations by adding triangle vertex offsets to base voxel coords, and final shading/ambient occlusion is calculated in the vertex shader [S1, unofficial].
+A real-time rendering pipeline that generates voxel terrain on the GPU, culls occluded voxels, and renders them using indirect instanced drawing [S1, unofficial]. It generates terrain as a giant array of voxels every frame, culls voxels by checking if they have all opaque neighbours, and uses `DrawIndirect` to render voxels [S1, unofficial]. The fragment shader computes vertex locations by adding triangle vertex offsets to base voxel coords, and final shading/ambient occlusion is calculated in the vertex shader [S1, unofficial].
 
 ### Voxel Culling and Visibility Computation
-A compute shader pass that identifies visible voxels from the dense grid and writes them to a sparse buffer, using an atomic counter to track the number of visible voxels [S1, unofficial]. It clears the count atomic buffer, executes the visibility pass with the same workgroup dispatch as generation, and copies the atomic count to the draw indirect buffer to set the instance count. A voxel is visible if it is on the boundary or has an empty von Neumann neighbour [S1, unofficial].
+A compute shader pass that identifies visible voxels from the dense grid and writes them to a sparse buffer, using an atomic counter to track the number of visible voxels [S1, unofficial]. It clears the count atomic buffer, executes the visibility pass with the same workgroup dispatch as generation, and copies the atomic count to the draw indirect buffer to set the instance count [S1, unofficial]. A voxel is visible if it is on the boundary or has an empty von Neumann neighbour [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity**: $O(N)$ where $N = CHUNK\_SIZE^3$ for generation. Culling is also $O(N)$ as it checks each voxel's neighbours [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity**: $O(N)$ for the dense voxel buffer. Culling adds $O(V)$ where $V$ is the number of visible voxels [S1, unofficial].
